%% What you built — Resilience, Multi-Cluster & DR wrap-up.
%% Application-level ladder from the lab: pod/node loss -> a whole site lost -> mesh failover
%% across sites -> RHSI links the sites -> survives a site loss, then a dotted line to the platform
%% DR net (concept, not graded). `direction LR` inside the `you` subgraph turns what was a
%% four-node `direction BT` column into one row; kept the real edges (not `~~~`) since their labels
%% carry the exercise mapping. Resized 2026-08-22: was 641x629 intrinsic (900x883 rendered, text at
%% 1.4x).
%% Follow-up 2026-08-22: `r4->net` crossed out of "you", silently disabling its `direction LR`
%% (900x1380 @2.11x, worse than before). Re-pointed at the container (`you->net`) — the label
%% already reads at the ladder level ("catastrophe beyond failover"), not about r4 specifically.
flowchart TB
  subgraph you["What you built (application level)"]
    direction LR
    r1["pod / node loss"] -->|"replicas · PDB · spread · HPA<br/>(in-site resiliency — ex 1)"| r2["a whole SITE lost"]
    r2 -->|"Service Mesh cross-site failover<br/>(stable endpoint · locality · outlier · retries — ex 2)"| r3["sites in different DCs"]
    r3 -->|"RHSI VAN links the sites<br/>(Site · Connector · Listener · Link — ex 3)"| r4["survives a site loss"]
  end
  net["platform DR net (concept): OADP restores data<br/>· GitOps re-materializes the platform"]
  you -.->|"catastrophe beyond failover"| net
  classDef a fill:#e6f4ea,stroke:#137333,color:#0d652d;
  classDef b fill:#fef7e0,stroke:#b06000,color:#7a4100;
  classDef c fill:#e3f2fd,stroke:#1565c0,color:#0d47a1;
  class r1 a; class r2,r3 b; class r4 c; class net c;
